Before anything is downloaded, exported or captured: will this capture run on this machine's
GPU?  xe-forge capture {{ args }}

The capture runs the model on token ids only, as a text-generating decoder. A model that
cannot run that way -- one that needs images or audio, an encoder-decoder -- does not fit:
say so. Otherwise answer from the model's config (the hub's metadata, no weight download),
the device's memory, and how this framework executes this model at this workload -- weights
in the requested format, KV cache for batch x (input + output) tokens, and the working
memory of its layers as the framework runs them. Do not run the model. Write fit.json
{"fits": true|false, "need_gb": <n>, "have_gb": <n>, "reason": "<one line>"}.
